BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 429.77 Tm (The most expensive failure the TEM operators report is the disconnect that never happened. Brightfin onboarded a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 414.55 Tm (client that had moved out of an office long ago and emailed the carrier to shut the switch off; it never got shut off,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 399.32 Tm (finance kept paying the invoices because it did not know the office had closed, and Brightfin recouped roughly $56,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 384.10 Tm (in erroneous billing [lxObl7Zpr2A @ 00:03:06]. Auditel hit the same pattern in its forward-savings work: lines with no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 368.87 Tm (use for months still billing, plus closed satellite offices whose services were never canceled, which it says happens) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 353.65 Tm (more than you might think [F00NVfaC6Tk @ 00:02:06]. Auditel adds that the order cycle itself is a trap, because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 338.42 Tm (providers sometimes place disconnect orders incorrectly or do not place them at all, and the accounts keep billing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 323.20 Tm (entire time, so orders must be monitored rigorously until the bill confirms the change [F00NVfaC6Tk @ 00:01:18].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 307.97 Tm (Ancy Alphonse describes the closed-site variant from the analyst chair: devices moved or ported to a different vendor,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 292.75 Tm (the building empty, yet charges persist on the invoice until someone works the vendor and discovers a modem still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 277.52 Tm (activated at the site [RV9K4EXWxJs @ 00:04:19].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 262.30 Tm (Auto-pay is where leakage hides. ExpenseSavvy says owners put vendors on auto pay and forget what they are paying,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.07 Tm (with no transparency into what the business down the street pays the same vendor for the same account) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.85 Tm ([2RDXap2GiBE @ 00:01:28]. Brightfin sizes the blind spot: 50 phones sitting in a closet at about $100 a month each is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 216.62 Tm (roughly $5,000 buried inside a $400,000 total charge, very easy to miss even a year after the employee left) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 201.40 Tm ([lxObl7Zpr2A @ 00:07:47]. Prior audits are no proof of a clean bill either. Auditel ran a go-behind audit on a client) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 186.17 Tm (that had been audited twice in the not-too-distant past, found multiple billing errors in data accounts overbilled for a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.95 Tm (very long time, and obtained a $165,000 credit on a single account [YAHf-FXxBCM @ 00:01:19]. The renewal desk is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 155.72 Tm (another leak: Auditel found a client that was not overcharged per se but was paying far more than it should after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 140.50 Tm (renewing without attention, and rate benchmarking cut rates, sometimes by more than 50% [F00NVfaC6Tk @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 125.27 Tm (00:01:49]. The fixed-line results show the scale: one account fell from $68,000 to just under $36,000 a month, and two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 110.05 Tm (others dropped from about $5,600 and $6,200 to a little over $900 each.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 94.82 Tm (In-house teams fail on bandwidth and memory. Single Source Telecom warns that staff must scour every bill, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 79.60 Tm (contact carriers and negotiate refunds, which can be the majority of project time, and they still need access to past and) Tj ET
