BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (SaaS Procurement Insider runs the sharpest usage math. Last login gets tracked, but login frequency is 'most important') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (and most audits miss it: a user logging in three times a year belongs on a restricted tier, and an average session of 90) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (seconds signals view-only use [udHdwtjP7yM @ 00:05:06]. The killer number is cost per active user, annual cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (divided by users with at least four logins in 90 days; in the worked example, a $30,000 contract becomes $1,071 per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (active user, with 122 people never touching it [udHdwtjP7yM @ 00:09:37]. Triage follows in three bands: below 20%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (usage gets a 30-day justification window and is otherwise cancelled, 20 to 70% gets right-sized with the vendor 90 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (out, and above 70% gets negotiated for escalation clauses and a flat renewal. CloudEagle's cut line is blunter: 'cancel) Tj ET
