BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (conservative on growth projections, and be aggressive with seat cuts because seats can be added back. Then anchor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (below the target, never lead with multi-year, push year-one pricing down first and only then trade a longer term for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (concessions; expect several rounds because the first counter is rarely the best [veu6EUBTdBE @ 00:04:24]. Redress) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (Compliance supplies the benchmark ammunition: almost nobody pays Oracle list price on large enterprise deals, and if) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (peers of similar size get 40% off an ERP cloud package, that becomes the baseline. Quote a competitor's number) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (directly, such as Workday's proposal, and collect at least three discount data points from peers, consultants, or RFPs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (before signing [sALcv-71Klw @ 00:00:36].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (Price-cap fine print is where renewal savings quietly die, and the practitioners map the traps clause by clause. Marcus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (Harris lists the standard conditions vendors attach: a minimum volume of the new purchase, a minimum spend that is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (separate from volume, excluded product lines, and a term-match rule where a five-year initial term cannot be renewed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (for one year and keep the cap, so the clever cap often covers nothing actually needed at renewal time [PQUXMXjSfjw) Tj ET
