BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 528.87 Tm (and a P90 user $21.00, a 5:1 spread sitting under a $29 price [ubYfOw6FSPA @ 00:11:51]. Flip the meter onto the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 513.65 Tm (customer and the blowups move to their side: a Cursor $7,000 annual plan consumed in one day, and Replit charging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 498.42 Tm ($1,000 a week against a usual $180 to $200 [ubYfOw6FSPA @ 00:15:39]. Umlauft adds that actual costs exceed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.20 Tm (vendor estimates by 30% to 50%, and buyers are pushing back [xmq83cmzth4 @ 00:04:03]. Garberson's fix is to watch) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 467.97 Tm (the top 10% of accounts by margin and split expansion revenue so you can see whether the unit is working. Hartuv's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 452.75 Tm (launch discipline is a fair-use policy to cap losses, then a pilot with 5 to 20 customers before measuring value and cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 437.52 Tm (Renewal uplifts leak quietly. MonetizeNow calls enforcement the tricky part under manual ops and says uplifts that are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 422.30 Tm (not automated simply get missed, which is revenue leakage [x0K0bAATQIA @ 00:03:28]. Their fix stores the uplift as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.07 Tm (a fixed or maximum percentage on the quote, so a $100 per user per month seat rolls to $105 automatically through an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 391.85 Tm (account-specific rate, and accepting the renewal blocks further amendments. Hartuv argues that uplift outweighs churn) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 376.62 Tm (by a multiple, points to Salesforce at 7% a year, and coaches founders to bake 3% to 7% into contracts, with the blunt) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 361.40 Tm (negotiating line: start at seven and then procurement will take you down to four [jOL79tUtq3o @ 00:31:08]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.17 Tm (price-cut trap runs the other way. Ulrik's warning is Rackspace, whose roughly 33% cut was simply matched by AWS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.95 Tm ([cdQzCVUJybY @ 00:07:15]. On the fee side, Willingness to Pay reports the upside of getting fairness right: an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 315.72 Tm (insurtech went from roughly 60M to roughly 100M DKK ARR on 30 customers by adding infrastructure fees, summed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 300.50 Tm (up as raising prices 60 with no churn [BGb6-WKMNN4 @ 00:29:59]. Uplift and fee lines only stick when they are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 285.27 Tm (written into the quote and the contract.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.05 Tm (Packaging and metric errors kill deals before price is ever discussed. Willingness to Pay saw the Lifegen density trap) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 254.82 Tm (firsthand: 1M cases at a ?20 average, but 700K of them were zero-value, which invites sorting of volume worth 1.4M) Tj ET
